BetterMacField contains the project's integration and launcher source code.
The MIT license applies to that source code. Identifiers, interface names,
layout information and short expected-byte fingerprints identify supported
client implementations; they do not represent ownership of the game.

Arknights: Endfield game content and trademarks belong to their respective
rights holders. PlayCover/PlayTools and Apple's Metal/MetalFX remain separate
components with their own terms. They are not bundled in this repository.

The local full-feature launcher package also contains rendering programs
prepared from a verified local game export: original GTAO/contact compute
programs and adapted lighting/character shader programs. These are build
inputs kept outside the tracked MIT source tree (build/Graphics), and are
not relicensed under MIT. No models, textures, Unity resource bundles, IPA
files, or MOD payloads are included in this launcher package. The current
packaging helper consumes a prepared local export; it is not yet a standalone
extractor for arbitrary player installations.

The optional native-assets vegetation package contains prepared scene chunks:
original iOS scene records plus selected PC-authored instance definitions,
placements and streaming ownership. Models, materials and textures are resolved
from the installed iOS client. These game-derived scene records are local build
inputs under build/Vegetation, excluded from the source repository and the MIT
license. prepare_vegetation.py and tools/scene_vegetation.py are build-tool source.
